## Post-merge verification harness correction

PR #99 is already merged to protected main at `a7d09f92b1f6085f74e69e0f4f2b754f566e3592`.

The merged application tree is byte-for-byte identical to the fully accepted PR #99 tree, and the pre-merge exact-head Level B gate passed.

The remaining post-merge issue is CI classification:

- squash merge removed `[level-b]` from the commit subject;
- the merged change spans multiple product scopes;
- `classify-verification.mjs` therefore returned `scope=full` but `level_b=false`;
- CI launched the entire 651-test browser suite unsharded in the 20-minute Level A job;
- GitHub cancelled it at test 575/651 due to the job time limit.

This PR makes any non-documentation `scope=full` change classify as Level B. Broad/multi-surface squash pushes will therefore use the existing sharded Level B verification path instead of the unsharded Level A fallback.

